# Steamworks: Networking and authentication

Use ISteamNetworkingMessages or ISteamNetworkingSockets instead of the old ISteamNetworking P2P API, and have a server verify every auth ticket before trusting the player it names.

## The old ISteamNetworking P2P API is used (warning)

- Why: Valve deprecated ISteamNetworking; ISteamNetworkingMessages and ISteamNetworkingSockets replace it with relayed, encrypted connections.
- Fix: Move SendP2PPacket/ReadP2PPacket to ISteamNetworkingMessages (closest) or ISteamNetworkingSockets.
- Source: https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/api/ISteamNetworking

## Auth tickets are created but not verified in this project (info)

- Why: A ticket proves who a player is only after a server checks it; trusting the client's word allows spoofing.
- Fix: Verify tickets on the server (BeginAuthSession, or ISteamUserAuth/AuthenticateUserTicket from a backend).
- Source: https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/features/auth

